# Git-LFS hook artifact. If core.hooksPath is ever set to the relative path
# "dev/null" (a Windows stand-in for /dev/null), `git lfs install` writes
# pre-push/post-checkout/post-commit/post-merge into a literal dev/null/
# directory in the working tree instead of .git/hooks/. Harmless but real, and
# a `git add -A` would publish it. There is no legitimate dev/null in this repo.
/dev/null
